{"kind":"request","text":"Archive parent read with a cost that does not grow with the archive.\n\nThe blob:none stopgap (ac1a5d6f) restores the Grow archive's parent read, but the host returns the wanted tree with every tree below it. The allowance for that reply is sized for one object (maximum + 8,192 bytes), so the root tree read refuses \"inflated bytes\" once all trees in the archive pass 8,487 bytes. The checker's reconstruction (d2a8427a) puts that at about 66 passes with no retained files, or about 25 with two retained files per pass. When it happens, every pass stops again with no fallback.\n\nMake the per-pass parent read cost independent of the number of passes in the archive. The checker named three directions: (a) keep hash-checked companion trees from the same reply, with an allowance from the v2 layout bounds (this cost still grows); (b) keep in native state what the next pass needs from the parent's path trees, so a pass reads no old trees from the host; (c) a host object read without a filter. The host refuses every filter but blob:none, and an unfiltered fetch returns blobs too (planner probe da1b3d2f). The planner prefers (b) if its state stays within the v2 layout bounds. Weigh the three in the note and say why you chose one.\n\nAcceptance: a test sends host-shaped blob:none replies (with companion trees) for an archive well past the stopgap bound, for example 200 passes with two retained files each, and every parent read succeeds within a fixed bound. A control at the stopgap code fails at the measured bound. The response guard and the existing byte limits do not widen. One gate before exact-head review. The planner deploys after approval.","body":{"conditions":"Per-pass parent-read cost independent of archive pass count; host-shaped blob:none test past the stopgap bound (200 passes, two retained files each); control fails at the measured bound; no widened guard or byte limit; one gate before exact-head review.","priority":"high","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}